  "methodology": "True high-precision Remez exchange on [-1,0], followed by nearest Q24 coefficient encoding. Degree six uses quadratic Horner; degree seven uses sequential Horner. Argument reduction and polynomial products use exact floor. Variants change only the four squaring roundings. Output witness is nearest-even integer to the verified Q48 numerator divided by S+E. Grid and random tests are samples; exhaustive, when present, covers all Q24 input encodings in [-16,16]. Float64 references are numerical checks, not a formal real-arithmetic error proof.",
  "range_proof": "For degree six, 0<=U=floor(T*T/S)<=-T<=S. The coefficients satisfy C4>=C5, C2>=C3, C2+C4+C6<=C1<=C0=S. Thus 0<=Q2<=C4+C6 and 0<=Q1<=C2+C4+C6<=C1, giving -C1*S<=C1*T+U*Q1<=0 and H in[0,S]. Nearest-square rescaling preserves[0,S]. Polynomial numerators have absolute value<=S*S, and square numerators<=S*S+S/2<2**62; denominator lies in[S,2S].",
